# Singles Day and Live Commerce
#
# How a student joke about the date 11.11 became the largest online sales festival, how streamer-sellers sold at that scale, and how regulators answered in 2021.

#>markets_singles_day
#:layer #!reference
#:domain #!markets
#:form #!dossier
#:level #!foundation
#:review #!spot_checked
#:valence #!bonk
#:era #!contemporary

^"emit"{
 ~#title: "Singles Day and Live Commerce"
 ~#claim: "Singles Day grew from a 1990s student custom into an Alibaba sales festival in 2009, livestream sellers sold at festival scale, and 2021 brought antitrust, marketing, and tax actions."
 ~#proof: "Dates and totals come from encyclopedia pages on Singles Day, Daniel Zhang, Alibaba, Viya, and HSN, marked as encyclopedia; the 2021 marketing measures are named from the writer and flagged."
 ~#door: "Read the origin, the scale, and the sellers, then the 2021 actions, and log one live selling stream with the kit."
 ~#audience: "readers new to live commerce and anyone comparing selling streams across platforms"
 continuity: "Singles Day and Live Commerce | festival scale"
 cold_open: "A student joke about a date grew to festival scale, and live sellers turned streams into storefronts until regulators stepped in."
}

